    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0082" n="8" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg8"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War/17332½: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d8-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">triple priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-11">December 11,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>To the President from the Former Naval
                        Person.</p>
                <p>I see reports that Admiral Leahy is to leave Vichy. Am most anxious to discuss
                    with you offering Vichy blessings or cursings on the morrow of a victory in
                    Libya. Trust your link with Pétain will not be broken meanwhile. We have no
                    other worthwhile connection.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d8-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d8-f1-content">
                <p>Sent as telegram 6012 over Winant’s signature to the Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
